          "type": "pin_functions",
          "params": {
            "description": "INT — Active-Low Interrupt (Open-Drain). Connect to an external voltage with a pullup resistor.",
            "source": "https://download.mikroe.com/documents/datasheets/MAX30102_datasheet.pdf (19-7740 Rev 1, p.8 Pin Description)"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "usage_note",
          "params": {
            "note": "Pulled low while an enabled interrupt is pending (FIFO almost full, new sample ready, ambient light cancellation overflow, die temperature ready) and on power-up (PWR_RDY, which cannot be disabled); cleared by reading the Interrupt Status registers 0x00-0x01. VOL <= 0.2 V at 6 mA. Needs an external pull-up (1 kohm to VDDIO in the application circuit).",
            "source": "https://download.mikroe.com/documents/datasheets/MAX30102_datasheet.pdf (19-7740 Rev 1, pp.4, 12-13, 31)"
          }
        }
